From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: psigod <psigod@example.com>
Date: Wed, 19 Nov 2026 20:30:00 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] clk: qcom: gcc-msm8996: 12.5 MHz for the fingerprint SPI

The Egis ET510 fingerprint sensor on BLSP1 QUP6 SPI runs at 12.5 MHz;
TrustZone drives the bus and reads the sensor to identify it. The shared
BLSP QUP SPI rate table has no 12.5 MHz entry, so a 12.5 MHz request
rounds up to the next rate, 15 MHz, overclocking the sensor: the
trustlet then cannot read it ("can't check sensortype"), the BAuth
session never opens and every fingerprint command is rejected. Add the
12.5 MHz rate (GPLL0 600 MHz / 12 * 1/4) that downstream uses here.

Signed-off-by: psigod <psigod@example.com>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 drivers/clk/qcom/gcc-msm8996.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/drivers/clk/qcom/gcc-msm8996.c b/drivers/clk/qcom/gcc-msm8996.c
index 1111111111aa..2222222222bb 100644
--- a/drivers/clk/qcom/gcc-msm8996.c
+++ b/drivers/clk/qcom/gcc-msm8996.c
@@ -446,6 +446,7 @@ static const struct freq_tbl ftbl_blsp1_qup1_spi_apps_clk_src[] = {
 	F(960000, P_XO, 10, 1, 2),
 	F(4800000, P_XO, 4, 0, 0),
 	F(9600000, P_XO, 2, 0, 0),
+	F(12500000, P_GPLL0, 12, 1, 4),
 	F(15000000, P_GPLL0, 10, 1, 4),
 	F(19200000, P_XO, 1, 0, 0),
 	F(25000000, P_GPLL0, 12, 1, 2),
-- 
